  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Local Gigantism is a rare congenital or acquired condition that can be caused by neurofibromatosis, proteus syndrome, amyloidosis, or tumor and presents with enlargement of a digit.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with relative enlargement of one or more of the toes. Radiographs are helpful for surgical planning.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally reconstruction or amputation if symptomatic or if leading to functional deficits.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
